                <pb facs="0433" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.516/294a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-06T16:00:00-04:00">June 6, 1934—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Lancaster advises us that the National City Bank is prepared to accede to the
                    request which it has received from Haiti to extend option for purchase of
                    National Bank of Haiti beyond June 1, but is cabling De la Rue to ask his
                    opinion whether as a matter of tactics it would not be advisable to limit such
                    extension at this time to 30 days.</p>
                <p>Please cable your views on this point.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
